cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OSF in your work, please cite the concept paper below."
title: "OSF — Open Streaming Format"
abstract: >-
  Open Streaming Format (OSF) is a binary, block-oriented file format for
  time-series measurement and process data, designed for embedded streaming
  write and fast block-wise read. The specification is published under CC BY
  4.0; reference implementations in Rust, Python, C++, Java and Delphi are
  MIT-licensed.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/optimeas/osf"
url: "https://docs.optimeas.com"
keywords:
  - measurement data
  - time series
  - streaming
  - file format
  - data integrity
authors:
